# UI icons: lucide-react-native only

All new and updated UI icons in this app use **`lucide-react-native`**, wrapped by [`src/components/ui/AppIcon.tsx`](../../src/components/ui/AppIcon.tsx). Aligns with minibot webui (`lucide-react`).

## Do

```tsx
import { House, MessageCircle } from "lucide-react-native";
import { AppIcon } from "@/components/ui/AppIcon";

<AppIcon icon={House} size={24} color={theme.text} />
```

- Pass a Lucide component as `icon={...}` (type `LucideIcon`).
- Prefer names that match webui when possible (`Settings`, `Plus`, `ChevronRight`, `Bot`, …).
- For selectable rows / dropdown options, store `icon: LucideIcon` on the option object (see `SettingsNavRow`).

## Don’t

- Do **not** add `@expo/vector-icons` (`Ionicons`, `MaterialIcons`, `MaterialCommunityIcons`) for new UI.
- Do **not** use `expo-symbols` / SF Symbol wrappers for UI icons.
- Do **not** import Lucide icons and render them raw in feature code when `AppIcon` fits—keep stroke/size defaults consistent.
